Algerians are voting in parliamentary elections on Thursday, with cost of living concerns, questions over political freedoms and the national football team’s World Cup run all competing for public attention.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/87002b0c-75e2-11f1-a0e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria2bis.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/87002b0c-75e2-11f1-a0e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria2bis.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">23d54ece-75e0-11f1-b2c6-e7d878263f35</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 07:12:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/87002b0c-75e2-11f1-a0e7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria2bis.jpeg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France confirms dates for 2027 presidential election</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260701-france-confirms-dates-for-2027-presidential-election-april-may</link><description>
France will hold the first round of its next presidential election on 18 April 2027 and the runoff on 2 May after the government formally approved the dates at Wednesday's cabinet meeting.
